# CareCopilot's Qwen3-8B variant (PRD §3, §35).
#
#   ollama create carecopilot-qwen3 -f ollama/Modelfile
#   LLM_MODEL=carecopilot-qwen3 docker compose up
#
# Optional. The stack runs on stock `qwen3:8b`; this exists to pin the
# sampling parameters that the agent's structured calls depend on, so that
# a change to Ollama's defaults cannot quietly alter routing behaviour.
#
# There is deliberately no SYSTEM instruction here. CareCopilot's system
# prompt is assembled per request in app/prompts/system.py, where it can
# carry the retrieval context boundaries that PRD §24 requires; baking a
# second, weaker one into the model would give the agent two sets of
# standing instructions and no way to tell which applied.

FROM qwen3:8b

# Near-greedy. Routing, tool-argument construction and SQL generation are
# classification tasks with one right answer, and PRD §27 measures them for
# accuracy — sampling variance there shows up as an eval score that moves
# without the code changing.
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

# Sized for the largest prompt the app builds: system instructions, up to
# eight reranked chunks (RAG_CONTEXT_TOKEN_BUDGET=3000), the conversation
# digest, and the tool catalogue. Qwen3 supports far more, but every token
# of context is memory the server holds per concurrent request.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Qwen3 is a hybrid-thinking model. Its <think> blocks are stripped at the
# provider boundary (app/llm/openai_compatible.py) because PRD §26 forbids
# surfacing chain-of-thought — so they cost latency and tokens and reach
# nobody. Turning them off here is the cheaper half of the same decision;
# the stripping stays regardless, since this Modelfile is optional and
# `/no_think` is not honoured by every Qwen3 build.
PARAMETER num_predict 1024

# --- Quantization (PRD §36 P3) ---------------------------------------- #
#
# The `FROM` tag above *is* the quantization choice: Ollama's `qwen3:8b` is
# Q4_K_M, roughly 5GB. It is a deployment decision rather than application
# code — nothing in the backend changes — so the lever is this line and
# OLLAMA_MODEL, not a setting.
#
#   qwen3:8b         Q4_K_M   ~5.2GB   the default; what compose pulls
#   qwen3:8b-q8_0    Q8_0     ~8.9GB   when 8-bit fidelity is wanted
#   qwen3:8b-fp16    FP16     ~16GB    reference quality, GPU only
#
# Measure before trading up. This project's structured calls — routing, tool
# selection, SQL — are constrained by JSON Schema at the decoding layer, so
# the failure quantization would cause is not malformed output but a *worse
# choice* inside a valid enum. That shows up in §27's router and tool
# accuracy and nowhere else, which is the number to compare across tags.
#
# vLLM takes the same decision as a flag instead:
#   vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --quantization awq --port 8001
